      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DANGEROUS (10) looks a standout here. He came from this barrier to win by more than 5m when resuming at this circuit and distance a fortnight ago, his first hitout since July's Inter Dominion series. He should only be better for that outing and looks a class above these. DESSIE GEE (8) was far from disgraced when 6m behind DANGEROUS last start and was runner-up at this circuit and distance prior. Draws wider but is ticking along well. SERG BLANCO NZ (1) hasn't performed to market expectations in two outings for Jason Grimson but has come from wider barriers each time. The ace draw gives him the chance to show his best. CAPTAIN BELLASARIO (6) has first four claims off a placing behind the flying Captains Knock two back.",
